<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8153" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circum-curro</span></b> , ĕre,
			v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to run round</i> or <i>about</i> (not
			ante-Aug.), <i><span class="en">Vitr. 4, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">circumcurrens linea,</span>”
				<i>the periphery</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 1, 10, 41</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">eam artem (rhetoricen) circumcurrentem
					vocaverunt. quod in omni materiā diceret,</span>”
				<i>universal</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Quint. 2, 21, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
